    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d216">

                <pb facs="0271" n="257" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg257"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.00/2445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-29T13:00:00-03:00">February 29,
                            1944—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:27 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>576. Embassy received yesterday note announcing assumption of Presidency by
                    Farrell similar to communication mentioned in Caffery’s 728, February 28, 7
                        p.m.<anchor n="82" xml:id="d216-f1"/> In view of Department’s
                        instructions<anchor n="83" xml:id="d216-f2"/> I am making no
                    acknowledgment.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Rio.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
